{"id": "Dd6vXHdT7Sq", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why does Maa Shailputri ride a bull? 🐂 The first form of Maa Durga, explained in 40 seconds.\n\nShailputri means “daughter of the mountain” (Shail = mountain, Putri = daughter). She is the first of the Navadurga, worshipped on Day 1 of Navratri.\n\nHer bull, Nandi, isn’t random. He stands for:\n💪 Strength\n⛰️ Stability\n🕉️ Steadfastness\n\nAnd when she rides him, it means something deeper: divine strength, gently guiding the mightiest forces on earth. That’s why Navratri begins with her: strong, steady, grounded.\n\nBut why does she hold a trishul and a lotus? That’s another story… and it’s in the book. 📖\n\n✨ The Navadurga Series by Rishi Katha: picture books for kids aged 4–8, one for each form of Maa Durga. Book 1: Shailputri, The Daughter of the Mountain.\n🎁 Set of 3 for ₹600 → rishikatha.com (link in bio)\n\n👉 Save this for Navratri and share it with a parent who tells bedtime stories.\n💬 Which form of Maa Durga should we explain next?\n\nFollow @therishikatha for more stories from Indian heritage.\n\n#Shailputri #Navratri #Navadurga #MaaDurga #Navratri2026 #HinduMythology #IndianMythology #Nandi #DurgaPuja #KidsBooksIndia #IndianParenting #MythologyForKids #StorytimeForKids #PictureBooks #RishiKatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1790785048, "like_count": 8369, "comment_count": 22, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1123319100651706a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 43.785, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr22-1.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQMI-8m7UmyV9bpF_ko0_Zo4CyYfY6kraWbfRmS0v16UNG-YiRTWSDzaTK6xP_gOgO7oP_P5KDBgVK57m23CNtqEOCzJ7la2jOSN3KQ.mp4?_nc_cat=101&_nc_oc=AdrEBK7-dRwGGpoWZYWl0_5JeaVXIwt6nh8sfxCv6cDaHb-0-3qVB4nzotRe2FLbp4Vfc22xcyvMXKy6A7KnMCyP&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_h